+A role file's step that instructs that role's own action is the role's duty, and the spec criterion that accepts it is its acceptance, not a restatement (owner ruling 2026-11-06, issue #640). A spec restating a spec, a role restating another role or a skill, and a step restating a condition an owner states elsewhere still block. Failure example: lane gh593 blocked agents/shaper.md step 3, "read `repair-specs` then and offer the owner that repair", twice as restating roles `#acceptance-shaper-repair`; the pointer it asked for sent the shaper out of its target repo to resolve a kit anchor.
 
-A change can pass one axis and fail the other:
+Search once per part of the rule: each label, value and term it fixes, one grep each, across docs, comments, docstrings, help text, test headers and eval descriptions. A restatement paraphrases, so one phrase finds a share. Failure example: lane gh157 wrote the report-field reader scope here; its first review found 4 restatements, the next two found 3 more (scripts/octo-feather-qa:333, tests/qa.sh:429, tests/lane-merge-ask.sh:106) and 1 more (evals/ladder/suite.json:4).
 
-- Code that follows every standard but implements the wrong thing → **Standards pass, Spec fail.**
